  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). We already have one vector $v=\u27e8-4,2,6\u27e9.$ Let's also use the displacement vector $\\overset{\\to }{UV}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{UV} & =\u27e82,-1,-3\u27e9-\u27e85,3,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-3,-4,-4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $u=\u27e85,3,1\u27e9$ of the point $U,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =u+sv+t\\overset{\\to }{UV} \\\\ r & =\u27e85,3,1\u27e9+s\u27e8-4,2,6\u27e9+t\u27e8-3,-4,-4\u27e9,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
